`s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 3 of 10` MEANS
    `s 2(1) "workman" Time in one salary period` WITH
        `time the person was required to work as a workman` IS 3
        `total time the person was required to work` IS 10

`s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 5 of 10` MEANS
    `s 2(1) "workman" Time in one salary period` WITH
        `time the person was required to work as a workman` IS 5
        `total time the person was required to work` IS 10

`s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 6 of 10` MEANS
    `s 2(1) "workman" Time in one salary period` WITH
        `time the person was required to work as a workman` IS 6
        `total time the person was required to work` IS 10

-- The proviso: deemed a workman "unless it can be established that the time ... as a workman in any one salary period ... has on no occasion amounted to or exceeded one-half of the total time".  Arguments: employed partly as a workman and partly in some other capacity; the salary periods.
-- src:697 | Provided that when any person is employed by any
-- src:698 | one employer partly as a workman and partly in some other
-- src:699 | capacity or capacities, that person is deemed to be a
-- src:700 | workman unless it can be established that the time during
-- src:701 | which that workman has been required to work as a
-- src:702 | workman in any one salary period as defined in Part 3 has
-- src:703 | on no occasion amounted to or exceeded one‑half of the
-- src:704 | total time during which that person has been required to
-- src:705 | work in such salary period;
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" proviso: the person is deemed to be a workman` TRUE (LIST `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 3 of 10`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" proviso: the person is deemed to be a workman` TRUE (LIST `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 3 of 10`, `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 5 of 10`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" proviso: the person is deemed to be a workman` TRUE (LIST `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 3 of 10`, `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 6 of 10`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" proviso: the person is deemed to be a workman` FALSE (LIST `s 2(1) "workman" test period with workman time 6 of 10`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: manual labour under a contract of service; a seafarer; a domestic worker; operates or maintains passenger-for-hire or commercial vehicles; clerical staff; partly manual and partly supervising a workman; the First Schedule's answer; the Minister has declared the person a workman; the proviso's answer.
-- src:676 | “workman” means —
-- src:678 | (a) any person, skilled or unskilled, who has entered into
-- src:679 | a contract of service with an employer pursuant to
-- src:680 | which he or she is engaged in manual labour,
-- src:681 | including any artisan or apprentice, but excluding
-- src:682 | any seafarer or domestic worker;
-- src:687 | (b) any person, other than clerical staff, employed in the
-- src:688 | operation or maintenance of mechanically‑propelled
-- src:689 | vehicles used for the transport of passengers for hire
-- src:690 | or for commercial purposes;
